Confirms the defect: "cam-target"'s bare-spawned fMP4-repackage task died on
the injected panic (`is_finished()=true`, the diagnostic line) and nothing
restarted it, so a fresh WebSocket connection made after the panic never
receives a second binary message (only whatever the connection already
buffered, if anything) within the harness's own timeout -- the test's own
"must still be flowing" assertion fails, exactly the observable "stops and
never resumes" this item's own plan text names. Re-run once more to rule out
a one-off timing fluke: same failure, same line, same message.

