Confirms the fix: with the real `spawn_supervised_with` pattern restored,
"cam-target"'s fMP4-repackage task panics once on its own 100th frame (the
`corvette-media-bridge unit="cam-target/fmp4-repackage" event=panic` line),
its supervisor immediately respawns it, and the fresh worker builds up a new
initialization segment and fragments from scratch -- a fresh WebSocket
connection made after the panic receives its init segment and at least one
further fragment well within the timeout, so all of this test's own
assertions pass: cam-target's WS output resumes (and stays resumed on a
second check after a further wait); cam-target's own MoQ-publish output
stayed reachable throughout; cam-healthy's MoQ-publish, fMP4-WS, and
RTSP-restream outputs all stayed reachable throughout -- confirming
INV-5(a)'s cross-unit isolation held unconditionally regardless of which run
was active, exactly as the plan's own text says it must (verified directly
by these same "unaffected throughout" assertions passing in both runs, not
inferred from the mutation's own pass/fail alone). Re-run once more to rule
out a one-off timing fluke: same pass, same log shape.

The recurring "WebSocket protocol error: Connection reset without closing
handshake" lines in both runs are this test harness's own connection
teardown (`fmp4_ws_output_is_flowing`'s test client is dropped without
sending a WebSocket close frame once it has read the messages it needed) --
an artifact of the test client, not a server-side defect; it appears
identically in both the BROKEN and RESTORED runs and for both cameras.

Full revert and re-verification
---------------------------------
After capturing both runs above:
  - `crates/corvette-media-bridge/src/ws_repackager.rs`'s injected panic
    (the `PANIC_AFTER_NTH_FRAME` static and its `if` block) was removed.
  - `crates/corvette-media-bridge/tests/g2_mutation_temp.rs` was deleted.

Confirmed clean afterward:

    $ grep -rn "PANIC_AFTER_NTH_FRAME\|cam-target\|G2_MUTATION_BARE_SPAWN" crates/corvette-media-bridge/src/ crates/corvette-media-bridge/tests/
    clean -- no mutation artifacts remain

    $ cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked
      -> clean: one pre-existing clippy::result_large_err warning from
         tokio-tungstenite's own fixed Callback trait signature (see this
         item's own commit message/report), 0 errors; unrelated to this
         mutation.
    $ cargo test --workspace
      -> every crate's test result line reported "ok", 0 failed.
